<title>UK: National Express yr pretax profits up 45 pct.</title>
<headline>National Express yr pretax profits up 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		32.8		   vs 27.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 8.1		    vs 7.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 11.5		   vs 10.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     60.1		   vs 41.5</p>
<p> Operating profit	 62.3		   vs 44.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   482.5		  vs 317.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 55.6 and 60.5 million stg and dividend of 11-11.3 pence.</p>
<p>Originally a coach and bus operator, National Express Plc has won five British passenger rail franchises over the last 12 months under the government privatisation of the former British Rail network.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
